{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Inscribed… and upon them…</b> One must understand the verse's saying <b>and upon them</b>. Behold, in parashat Tissa (Exodus 31:18) I explained the statement ״inscribed by the finger of Elohim״ — that HaShem directed the finger of Elohim opposite the tablet in the shape of the letter, and through this the part opposite it was supported on the sides and a hollowed-out space remained, as in the verse's saying ״engraved on the tablets.״ Scripture now comes and informs us that the place of the engraving was hollowed out from the substance of the tablet, but the radiance of the light that flashed from the light of the finger of Elohim appeared as letters on high, though they were engraved — and this is what it says: <b>and upon them, according to all the words that HaShem spoke</b> etc. — meaning, just as one imagines that the speech was formed from it as a holy creation, so too, by the touch of Elohim upon the tablet, light was hewn and ascended over the tablets. Understand this."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:21.576750444Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}